---
/**
 * "How it works" — the DeskScene hero as a homepage section (E010 §2.3 copy,
 * DESIGN.md §8). One eyebrow, one H2, one line, the scene; the WebP is the
 * no-JS fallback. Buttons switch the state; callouts explain the product parts.
 */
import DeskScene from '../scene/DeskScene';
---
<section id="how-it-works" class="report-container pb-16 md:pb-20">
  <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-brand-text">How it works</p>
  <h2 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">Plug in. It watches two things. It nudges, then checks.</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] text-lg leading-8 text-ink-muted">
    The laser measures desk height, so it knows sitting from standing. The app watches keyboard and
    mouse activity, so it knows if you are there.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <noscript>
      <img
        src="/images/scene/desk-scene.webp"
        alt="A height-adjustable desk with a matchbox-sized sensor under the top, a laser beam to the floor, a monitor showing the desk height and a nudge, and a person at the desk"
        width="960"
        height="600"
        loading="lazy"
        style="width: 100%; border-radius: 28px;"
      />
    </noscript>
    <DeskScene client:visible />
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-muted">
    After 40 minutes of sitting, a small card in the corner. When the desk rises, it sees it.
    Every minute up buys back two minutes of sitting.
  </p>
</section>
